[{"sha":"d5d17ceccc00ca0cdc202a79b8d563e190127457","node_id":"C_kwDOEFLz89oAKGQ1ZDE3Y2VjY2MwMGNhMGNkYzIwMmE3OWI4ZDU2M2UxOTAxMjc0NTc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/d5d17ceccc00ca0cdc202a79b8d563e190127457","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/d5d17ceccc00ca0cdc202a79b8d563e190127457","author":{"name":"Sarcouy","email":"sarcouy@protonmail.com","date":"2026-09-27T17:06:24Z"},"committer":{"name":"Sarcouy","email":"sarcouy@protonmail.com","date":"2026-09-27T17:06:24Z"},"tree":{"sha":"9066c6633712f9e7df697b0b18c8d837080db44e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/trees/9066c6633712f9e7df697b0b18c8d837080db44e"},"message":"state: send a node its own self after its routes change\n\nThe mapper only adds the self node to a response when the change's\nOriginNode is the receiving node. SetApprovedRoutes always returned a\nbare PolicyChange, so the approved node never learned its routes on its\nlive map session: Self.AllowedIPs stayed without them and `tailscale\nstatus` never showed \"offers exit node\" until tailscaled restarted.\n\nSince 0.29.4 HasPolicyChange also compares exit routes, so a node\nwithdrawing and re-advertising them ends in a bare PolicyChange from\nUpdateNodeFromMapRequest instead of NodeAdded(id), which closed the only\nworkaround short of a restart.\n\nKeep the origin on both changes, as SetNodeTags does since #2996, so the\nmapper answers the node with its self next to the recompute. Peers keep\nreceiving the same policy response.\n\nFixes #3502\n\n🤖 Généré avec Claude Code","parents":[{"sha":"53113e2a67dbde9a7f5d27c049a631384968934c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/git/commits/53113e2a67dbde9a7f5d27c049a631384968934c","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/commit/53113e2a67dbde9a7f5d27c049a631384968934c"}],"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null},"event":"committed"},{"id":31941106